SIM-10: include the pattern start in the time to the next pattern period

timestep() finds the next pattern period n from Htime + Pstart, as
demands() does, but then took the time to it as n*Pstep - Htime, which
leaves out Pstart. With a pattern start that is not a multiple of the
pattern step, the step ended on a multiple of Pstep in simulation time
instead of at the pattern boundary, so each demand change was applied
late, at the next hydraulic step.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-10_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/hydraul.c b/src/hydraul.c
index fa96868..e7ac967 100755
--- a/src/hydraul.c
+++ b/src/hydraul.c
@@ -665,7 +665,7 @@ long  timestep(Project *pr)
     // Revise time step based on time until next demand period
     // (n = next pattern period, t = time till next period)
     n = ((time->Htime + time->Pstart) / time->Pstep) + 1;
-    t = n * time->Pstep - time->Htime;
+    t = n * time->Pstep - (time->Htime + time->Pstart);
     if (t > 0 && t < tstep) tstep = t;
 
     // Revise time step based on time until next reporting period
